id: decisions/050-extension-discipline
title: "One extension bag, always namespaced"
kind: decision-frame
record_shape: header
status: draft
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Claude Code session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-12; drafted from the JUDGMENTS.md reversal axis 'extension-discipline'; recommendation is an attributed inference and ratifies nothing"
version: "1.0.0"
updated: 2026-09-12
template_ref: templates/decision.yawn
principal_ref: principal:dave

axis: extension-discipline
axis_gloss: "whether extension points must be namespaced and bounded, or records may add arbitrary keys wherever they like"
poles:
  a: namespaced-bounded-extension
  b: free-key-extension
split: lone-exception
draft_status: full
leverage: 1.9
leverage_formula: "judgments_resolved(4) x split_weight(0.4) x authored_conflict_bonus(1.2)"

question: >
  Must every extension key be namespaced, including in the stable observation
  record, or may observation.v1 keep its looser key pattern?

why_it_matters: >
  Two written rules and one passing test say extension keys are reverse-DNS
  namespaced so they can never be mistaken for core fields or carry authority;
  observation.v1, the one stable schema, accepts a bare key like audit. A bot
  writing observations inherits either the namespaced bag or a loophole in the
  most-used record; a child Yawn learns which pattern to copy.

state_snapshot:
  description: >
    3 judgments sit at namespaced-bounded-extension (2 authored) and 1 at
    free-key-extension (0 authored). The repository asserts both directions on
    this axis.
  attributed_to: TAXONOMY.md
  epistemic_status: observed
  source_refs:
    - JUDGMENTS.md
    - TAXONOMY.md

lacuna:
  kind: unselected_choice
  description: >
    Whether a schema marked v1 may be tightened in place or only by shipping v2;
    the repo has no written versioning policy for schemas.

options:
  - name: A
    description: >
      Every extensions map in schemas/ uses one shared ExtensionBag definition: keys
      must be namespaced (at least one dot- or dash-separated segment) and
      extensions may never widen authority, privacy, proof or append-only
      invariants.
    cost: "Changing one propertyNames pattern in schemas/observation.v1.schema.json (or $ref-ing the holarchy ExtensionBag); fixtures/observation.v1.json has extensions: {} so nothing breaks."
    risk: "A downstream writer of observation.v1 with bare keys would fail on upgrade; none exists in the repo."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "Extend tests/observation-state-v1.test.mjs with the same two cases tests/agency-holarchy-v0.2.test.mjs already runs: org.example.audit accepted, not_namespaced rejected."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0826"
      - "J1062"
      - "J1206"
  - name: B
    description: >
      Extension keys are any token up to 200 characters; namespacing is advice in a
      $comment.
    cost: "Loosening the holarchy ExtensionBag pattern and deleting the not_namespaced rejection test."
    risk: "An extension key shadows a core field name in a later schema version; extension data carries permission, which J0826 forbids in five templates."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "None; B is honoured by removing a passing test."
    evidence_for:
      - "J1063"
  - name: C
    description: >
      Option A for every draft schema; observation.v1 keeps its pattern as versioned
      legacy until observation.v2, named in a shrink-only ledger with a date.
    cost: "One ledger entry; the same test as A with observation.v1 excluded."
    risk: "The most-used stable record is the one with the loophole, for as long as v2 does not ship."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "Same test as A with a one-entry GRANDFATHERED set."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0826"
      - "J1062"
      - "J1206"
      - "J1063"

recommendation:
  option_ref: A
  confidence: 0.8
  epistemic_status: inferred
  authority: none
  reasoning: >
    Two authored judgments and one proof-attached test are on A; the lone
    exception is a schema pattern nobody argued for, in a record whose only
    fixture has an empty extensions map, so tightening it costs one line and
    breaks nothing that exists. C only earns its keep if Dave holds that a v1
    schema may never be tightened in place, which no record states.

target_condition:
  mode: decide
  proposed_by: agent-on-behalf
  affected_principals:
    - principal:dave
  ratification_status: proposed
  sufficient_when:
    - "schemas/observation.v1.schema.json extensions propertyNames pattern equals the holarchy ExtensionBag pattern or $refs a shared definition"
    - "tests/observation-state-v1.test.mjs rejects a bare extension key and accepts a namespaced one, and passes"
    - "npm test stays green on the existing observation fixture"

choice:
  selected_by: ""
  option_ref: ""
  authority_ref: ""

proof:
  covers:
    - target_condition
    - options
  falsifier: >
    A record or fixture with a bare extension key under an observation passes
    validation.
  status: proposed

evidence_sample:
  - "J0826"
  - "J1062"
  - "J1206"
  - "J1063"

boundary:
  - "confidence cannot ratify an objective; this record proposes and Dave decides"
  - "the REVEALED judgments cited here describe what artifacts do, not what Dave chose"

source:
  template: templates/decision.yawn
  axis: TAXONOMY.md
  inventory: JUDGMENTS.md
  id_index: TAXONOMY.md
